{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"VERIFIED ON THE LIVE BOX — signing now works.\n\nAfter change 1570 merged and autodeploy rebuilt the review-bot image:\n  ssh-keygen: /usr/bin/ssh-keygen   (was: MISSING)\n\nRe-ran the IDENTICAL in-process probe that previously failed, inside the running container:\n  author      : Rebar Bot\n  author_email: joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com\n  author_id   : 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\n  author_sig  : PRESENT          <- was ABSENT / SshKeygenUnavailable\n  VERDICT: SIGNING WORKS\n\nAll three defects are closed:\n  1. no global git identity  -> author_id null -> signing skipped silently   [89128b2e09]\n  2. key not mounted         -> host path unreadable in container            [89128b2e09]\n  3. ssh-keygen absent       -> SSHSIG raises -> caught -> unsigned          [1570]\n\nCAVEAT ON THE EVIDENCE: the probe drives the real signing seam (_seam._apply_authorship) with\nthe real config, real key and real identity in the real container, and produces a real DSSE\nsignature — but it is in-process and writes nothing to the store. A genuine end-to-end event\nhas not been observed yet because the bot only writes when a review runs and there has been no\norganic review activity since the deploy. A watcher is confirming the first real post-deploy\nevent from env b2b5c498 carries author_sig."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786307372151221001,"uuid":"dc1a1553-e6ce-423f-b631-cf5c3b065e28"}